[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3874149551","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116113#issuecomment-3874149551","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116113","id":3874149551,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7m6tSv","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T22:13:58Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T22:52:35Z","body":"I cannot determine your ideal animation state from the MRP. However, I can confirm that the following error is occurring.\n\n```\nERROR: Condition \"!process_state->tree->property_parent_map.has(node_state.base_path)\" is true.\n```\n\nTo be clear, regarding the reported issue, are the following two points correct?\n\n- The problem only occurs when using BlendSpace's Capture mode\n- The problem only occurs at the exact moment the error appears\n\nIf that's the case, I think it might be fixed by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112308 since it has side effects that make instance access safer.\n\nOr, if you intend to synchronize time across different States using DiscreteCarry, I consider this an intended behavior rather than a bug. This is because BlendSpace's DiscreteCarry synchronizes the animation time within the BlendSpace itself, not time outside of it. If this use case is intended, I assume a more semantic Sync option is needed for StateMachine.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3874149551/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3875731175","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116113#issuecomment-3875731175","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116113","id":3875731175,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nAvbn","user":{"login":"MStellinga","id":3314522,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTQ1MjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3314522?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga","html_url":"https://github.com/MStellinga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T06:59:57Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T06:59:57Z","body":"Yes, it's only with capture (so maybe I'm misunderstanding something about that in this is expected behavior, in which case apologies).\n\nI've attached a video of what happens. The example project is set up so that whenever the animation travels from short to long the 'lenghten' animation plays and whenever the animation travels from long to short the 'shorten' animation plays. Left-right is by parameter of the blendspace.\n\nSo in the video, the sequence skips some of the shorten and lengthen animations. \nHere is the entire sequence, with the missing animations in brackets:\nshortR-shortL-lengthen-longL-shorten-shortL-lengthen-longL-longR-[shorten]-shortR-[lengthen]-longR-longL-[shorten]-shortL-[lengthen]-longL- shorten-shortL\n\nIk skips 4 times at around 18, 22, 26, and 29 seconds\n\nThe error occurs twice, so it's not a one-on-one match, but it might be related?\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d9af0e5f-ef7e-47ad-b022-2e7124754e2a","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3875731175/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3881682638","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116113#issuecomment-3881682638","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116113","id":3881682638,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nXcbO","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T01:53:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T02:07:55Z","body":"Alright, I understand.\n\nTo summarize the issue: “When switching to an animation that has already finished within the BlendSpace due to DC mode, this process occurs after the Reset processing of the StateMachineTransition. As a result, the remaining time is immediately set to 0, causing the State to be considered finished immediately\".\n\nTherefore, I assume this can be fixed by performing the Reset after the DC mode transition when it is requested upstream. However, since this could have significant impact, I think we need to test it carefully. In particular, since I expect this seek order issue likely exists in OneShot and Transition as well, we need to consider their consistency.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3881682638/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3882705020","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116113#issuecomment-3882705020","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116113","id":3882705020,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nbWB8","user":{"login":"MStellinga","id":3314522,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTQ1MjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3314522?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga","html_url":"https://github.com/MStellinga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MStellinga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T06:58:34Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T06:58:34Z","body":"That sounds right. But I don't know how this is supposed to work, so like I said, maybe I'm using it wrong. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3882705020/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]